* START-HISTORY:
* 26 Oct 26 dm  New.  The owner's decision of 26 Oct 2026 (S.76): SDSYS may have more than one session at a time, and that must be visible - an audit line when a
*               second one signs on (LOGIN), a mark on the rows of TOOL.SESSIONS, a count on the home screen's signed-on line.  This is the one definition of "a session
*               of SDSYS" the three of them use.
* 10 Nov 26 Windows port - from Linux 13d30532 (S.76), unchanged.  The TUI carry (f55e5fa5, RELEASE_1.1 197) brought its two callers, TOOL_HOME and TOOL_SESSIONS,
*               and not this file, so HOME in SDSYS stopped with "Unable to load '!sdsysn' object code at line 800 of $tool_home".  K$USERS.DEV is the
*               session's ttyname() (kernel.c), which MSYS2 fills for a console and leaves empty for piped input, so "on a terminal" means what it means on Linux.
*               LOGIN's half of S.76 was carried on 12 Nov 26 (RELEASE_1.1 252): LOGIN calls this when SDSYS signs on, so it is on BBPROC's bootstrap list.
* END-HISTORY
*
* START-DESCRIPTION:
*
*    CALL !SDSYSN(n, uids, mine, mytty)
*
*    n      how many sessions of the account SDSYS are on a terminal - the ones a person sits at.  A phantom, an API or SDNet process, a session that is being
*           logged out, and a session with no terminal (a piped command, SD -INTERNAL, a program started from a script) are not counted.
*    uids   their user numbers, a field mark between each
*    mine   1 when the calling session is one of them (its own account is SDSYS in the user table); at sign-on it may not have entered its account yet
*    mytty  1 when the calling session is on a terminal
*
* END-DESCRIPTION
*
* START-CODE

$internal
$no.xref
subroutine sdsysn(n, uids, mine, mytty)
$catalog !SDSYSN

$include syscom.h
$include keys.h
$include int$keys.h

   n = 0
   uids = ''
   mine = 0
   mytty = 0
   users = kernel(K$USERS, 0)
   for i = 1 to dcount(users, @fm)
      uv = users<i>
      uid = uv<1, K$USERS.UID> + 0
      has.tty = (uv<1, K$USERS.DEV> # '')
      if uid = @userno then mytty = has.tty
      flg = uv<1, K$USERS.FLAGS> + 0
      if downcase(uv<1, K$USERS.ACCOUNT>) = 'sdsys' and has.tty then
         if not(bitand(flg, USR$PHANTOM)) and not(bitand(flg, USR$SDVBSRVR)) and not(bitand(flg, USR$SDNET)) and not(bitand(flg, USR$LOGOUT)) then
            n += 1
            uids<-1> = uid
            if uid = @userno then mine = 1
         end
      end
   next i
   return
end

* END-CODE
